# BrainRace frontend configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The base URL of the backend API the frontend talks to. Every request is
# built as `${VITE_API_BASE_URL}/api/...`, so no code change is needed to
# point the frontend at a different backend.
#
# Default when unset or blank: the deployed Render backend
#   https://brain-race.onrender.com
# That default is what the production build relies on, so leave this variable
# unset there.
#
# For local development it MUST be set to your local backend:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
# Otherwise the local frontend silently talks to the deployed backend and
# ignores your local backend and its backend/.env entirely (symptoms: "this
# server has no ADMIN_USERNAME / ADMIN_PASSWORD configured", "OAuth is not
# configured", "email delivery is not configured").
#
# Vite loads .env.local in every mode, including `npm run build`, and
# .gitignore excludes *.local, so .env.local never reaches the deployed build.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is a PUBLIC frontend variable. Vite inlines VITE_* values into the
# JavaScript bundle that every visitor downloads, so they are visible to
# anyone. Never put secrets, API keys, tokens, or credentials here. Backend
# secrets belong in backend/.env, which is gitignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
